  "description": "Reid Let’s MTB | Affordable electric mountain bike\nAffordable electric assistance for off-road adventures – the Reid Let’s MTB combines trail-ready features with practical performance for budget-conscious riders.\nThe Reid Let’s MTB is designed for riders who want to explore off-road trails and tackle varied terrain with the added support of electric assistance. Combining accessible pricing with reliable components, it offers a practical entry point into electric mountain biking.\nA 250W motor with five levels of pedal assistance helps you tackle climbs and enjoy longer rides, while the integrated 375Wh battery provides power for exploring trails and countryside routes. Shimano 7-speed gearing offers straightforward, reliable shifting to help you adapt to changing terrain.\nTektro HD-M275 hydraulic disc brakes deliver controlled stopping power when navigating descents and uneven surfaces, helping you maintain confidence throughout your ride. With its focus on essential trail-riding features and everyday usability, the Let’s MTB makes electric-assisted off-road cycling more accessible.\nWhether you're new to mountain biking or looking for an affordable way to explore further, the Let’s MTB offers a practical combination of electric assistance, reliable components and off-road versatility.\nThe Let’s MTB is ideal for:\n\nBudget-conscious riders looking for an accessible entry into electric mountain biking\n\nOff-road beginners, with electric assistance to help make trail riding more manageable\n\nRiders tackling hills and varied terrain, with a 250W motor and five levels of pedal assistance\n\nLonger trail adventures, with an integrated 375Wh battery\n\nReliable gear changes, with Shimano 7-speed gearing for climbs and descents\n\nControlled braking on the trails, with Tektro HD-M275 hydraulic disc brakes\n\nRiders looking for affordable adventure, with practical features designed for exploring off-road routes\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
